            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0834" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660f.116Auto/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gittings</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-24T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                                1928—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received November 24—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>79. Regarding automobile contingent situation. Does Department wish me to file
                    written protest against delay in answering last note? If so, please instruct and
                    outline. Fault lies with Ministry of Commerce, and with all due allowances I
                    feel the delay now approaches point of discourtesy, not to mention further
                    injury to automobile business due to continued uncertainty. Commercial Attaché
                    agrees with this and reports only about 100 licenses issued so far since
                    November 5, beginning of new contingent year; also several hundred cars held in
                    customs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gittings</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
